essential component of the positive-feedback loop that maintains leading-edge structure and activity in macrophages</article-title><source>Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences, USA</source><year>2007</year><volume>104</volume><fpage>16176</fpage><lpage>16181</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Feij&#x000f3;</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Malh&#x000f3;</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Obermeyer</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Ion dynamics and its possible role during <italic>in vitro</italic> pollen germination and tube growth</article-title><source>Protoplasma</source><year>1995</year><volume>187</volume><fpage>155</fpage><lpage>167</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Franklin-Tong</surname><given-names>VE</given-names></name><name><surname>Dr&#x000f8;bak</surname><given-names>BK</given-names></name><name><surname>Allan</surname><given-names>AC</given-names></name><name><surname>Watkins</surname><given-names>PAC</given-names></name><name><surname>Trewavas</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Growth of pollen tubes of <italic>Papaver rhoeas</italic> is regulated by a slow-moving calcium wave propagated by inositol 1,4,5-trisphosphate</article-title><source>The Plant Cell</source><year>1996</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>1305</fpage><lpage>1321</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12239415</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Frech</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Andjelkovic</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Ingley</surname><given-names>E</give